==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Egg: N103''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gas Mask Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Gas Mask Cat is a powerful meatshield that can tank up to '''71.4k''' damage from Dark enemies at level 30 (with all three [[Void Fruit]]s maxed). Although Dark enemies are notorious for their high DPS typically denying these options, anti-Dark meatshields have definitively proven their place in the meta, namely [[Li'l Gau (Rare Cat)|Li'l Gau]] and [[Nono (Rare Cat)|Nono]]. Incidentally, Gas Mask Cat serves a partially similar purpose to Nono, acting as a secondary defense. Its very long standing range as a meatshield means it will stand behind your meatshields and hold ground as an emergency defense in case Dark enemies break through, providing grace time to get things back under control. Because of this, its longer recharge time for a meatshield can be forgiven.

It's important to note that Gas Mask Cat has higher range than [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], meaning a breakthrough will kill off your Bombercats before your Gas Mask Cats, so you might prefer using other anti-Dark meatshields at times. Against non-Dark Behemoths, it is only able to tank 23.8k damage, but a whopping '''119k''' damage against [[Ragin' Gory]], [[Crocodylidae Kurocroc]], and [[Casaurian Darkjo]], who it also counters with its Toxic immunity.

